-- title:
--   Supersingular reduced field as a Drinfeld quotient field, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $\ell g$ be a prime with $\ell g\equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell g\mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $q$ is a nonunit, let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over the residue field $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\kappa$), assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and fix $s\in W$. Let $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ be an intermediate field over $\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element of $A$ such that $A\cap k_0$ is a Henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and algebraically closed residue field, and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$. Let $K_b$ be the intermediate field $\bot$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $k_0$ and $A_b$ the valuation subring of $K_b$ cut out by $A$, assumed a Henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by a nonzero $\varpi_b$. Give $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ the $k_0$-algebra structure coming from $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\subseteq\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$. The assertion is: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $k_0$ and every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is everything, $W_0$ contracts to $A$ on $k_0$, $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, and the image of $\pi_0$ generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$; and for every subring $B\subseteq\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ equipped with an $A_b$-algebra structure whose structure map is the inclusion $A_b\subseteq K_b\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\to\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, with $B$ contained in $W_0$, with $W_0$ consisting exactly of the quotients $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and the image of $\varpi_b$ not dividing $h$, with $B$ stable under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for all $\zeta:\mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and all $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and such that for every $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every witness that $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$ is a domain and every $\zeta$ there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho:B\to\mathrm{DrinfeldCurve.quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ with $\#C_s=\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$, kernel the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$, agreeing on $A_b$ with reduction to $\kappa$ followed by the structure map, with every element of the quotient field a ratio of two $\rho$-values with nonzero denominator, with image exactly the elements of $\mathrm{quotField}$ lying in the image of $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$ in the Drinfeld function field, and $\rho$ intertwining $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$ with $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}\,q\,\kappa$ at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ — then for every field $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$ and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with reduced field $F_{ss}$ (a valuation subring of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ contracting to $A$ on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with a surjective residue map onto $F_{ss}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal and which is compatible with reduction on $A$) whose ring of integers meets $F_0$ in exactly $W_0$, the following holds: for every $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every witness that $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$ is a domain and every $\zeta:\mathrm{Idx}\,q$ there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity with $\#C_s=\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e:F_{ss}\cong\mathrm{DrinfeldCurve.quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ which carries, for each $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $R$'s integers through $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$ and with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)\in\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$, the induced automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}$ of $F_{ss}$ to the action of $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ on the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   This is the $q=2$ form, at the rigidifying auxiliary level provided by a prime $\ell g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the identification of the reduced residue field at a supersingular point of the semistable model with the fixed field of a subgroup of $\mu_{q+1}$ inside the function field of the Drinfeld curve, together with the matching of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-level automorphisms with the Drinfeld action. It transfers the data of an affine chart $B$ with its specialisation $\rho$ to the intrinsic reduced field of a regular prolongation, and feeds the construction of the local stalks of the semistable model at supersingular points.
